Build array where you can find maximum exactly k comparison

You are building an array of size n, each number between 1 to m.
A comparison cost increases whenever your new element becomes a new maximum.

Example:
Array = [2, 3, 1, 5]
Maximum updates → 2 → 3 → 5 → cost = 3

Goal:
👉 Count how many arrays of size n have exactly K max-updates (search_cost).

At each position in the array, you choose a value from 1 to m.

Two things matter:

What is the current maximum so far?
This decides whether the next value increases the cost.
How many max-updates have happened already?

So for each new number we choose:
If it is greater than current max,
→ new maximum found → cost increases by 1

Otherwise
→ cost stays the same

Choice at each step

For each possible next value val from 1 to m:

Case 1: val > max_so_far
→ It becomes the new maximum
→ cost increases
→ next state:
solve(idx+1, val, cost_so_far + 1)

Case 2: val <= max_so_far
→ No new max
→ cost unchanged
→ next state:
solve(idx+1, max_so_far, cost_so_far)

We sum both results.

🧱 Base Case

When idx == n:
If we reached exactly k cost → valid array → return 1
Otherwise → return 0

class Solution {
public:
    int mod = 1e9+7;
    int t[51][101][51];

    int solve(int n, int m, int k, int idx, int max_ele, int search_cost){

        if(search_cost > k) return 0;

        if(idx == n){
            return search_cost == k;
        }

        if(t[idx][max_ele][search_cost] != -1) 
            return t[idx][max_ele][search_cost];

        long long result = 0;

        for(int val = 1; val <= m; val++){

            if(val > max_ele){
                // new maximum found
                result += solve(n, m, k, idx+1, val, search_cost+1);
            } else {
                // no new max
                result += solve(n, m, k, idx+1, max_ele, search_cost);
            }

            result %= mod;
        }

        return t[idx][max_ele][search_cost] = result;
    }

    int numOfArrays(int n, int m, int k) {
        memset(t, -1, sizeof(t));
        return solve(n, m, k, 0, 0, 0);
    }
};


